Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-rs6000.c
Line: 2063
Function: xcoff_write_armap_big
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: The loop condition uses while (map[i].abfd == current_bfd) without checking i < orl_count. When i is incremented to orl_count, the next condition evaluation reads map[orl_count], an out-of-bounds access. This can occur when processing the final group of entries for a member.

Source context:
